From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000011 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: polyregion <noreply@polyregion>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [SPIRV] move the assign-type record when replacing memory
 instructions

replaceMemInstrUses rebuilds the spv_assign_type user for the replacement and
erases both the old user and the old instruction, but leaves the registry
record keyed by the erased instruction pointing at the erased assign-type
call. Once the allocator hands either address to a new value, a lookup
(e.g. buildAssignPtr) returns the stale call and updateAssignType rewrites
argument 1 of whatever call now lives there. A cmpxchg followed by
extractvalue hits this: the spv_extractv index becomes `metadata i32 poison`
and instruction selection asserts in foldImm. Whether it happens depends on
heap address reuse, so it is intermittent and host dependent. Move the
record to the replacement before rebuilding the users, as
replaceAllUsesWith already does.

Not upstream as of llvm/llvm-project main (2026-10-25).
---
 llvm/lib/Target/SPIRV/SPIRVEmitIntrinsics.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/llvm/lib/Target/SPIRV/SPIRVEmitIntrinsics.cpp b/llvm/lib/Target/SPIRV/SPIRVEmitIntrinsics.cpp
--- a/llvm/lib/Target/SPIRV/SPIRVEmitIntrinsics.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Target/SPIRV/SPIRVEmitIntrinsics.cpp
@@ -1372,6 +1372,7 @@
 void SPIRVEmitIntrinsics::replaceMemInstrUses(Instruction *Old,
                                               Instruction *New,
                                               IRBuilder<> &B) {
+  GR->updateIfExistAssignPtrTypeInstr(Old, New, true);
   while (!Old->user_empty()) {
     auto *U = Old->user_back();
     if (isAssignTypeInstr(U)) {
